<title>BRAZIL: Banco do Brasil trading to resume Friday.</title>
<headline>Banco do Brasil trading to resume Friday.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade in Brazilian federal bank Banco do Brasil will resume today on local stock exchanges, said a spokeswoman for the Sao Paulo bourse.</p>
<p>Banco do Brasil shares had been suspended on Thursday because of the announcement of the bank's 1996 results.</p>
<p>Banco do Brasil posted a record 7.5 billion reais loss last year. On Wednesday's close, the bank's preferred shares traded at 10 reais on the Sao Paulo bolsa.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Rio de Janeiro Newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
</text>
